// A parity echo above a long wall; the seed is below it.
name Choir Stalls
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hint The seed lies along this bottom row. The echo rose beyond the long wall, which is open at both ends.
tip The origin sits in the middle of the small cross at the echo's centre.
intro A long wall with the echo behind it and the seed before it. The wall is open at both ends, as walls that outlast their makers tend to be.
outro Odd numbers make the choir. The centre holds the note.
